+
+
+## Experimental hybrid FlyDSL MLA prefill
+
+The explicit `ROCM_AITER_FLYDSL_MLA` attention backend and
+`ROCM_AITER_FLYDSL_FP8` MLA prefill backend provide a native port of an
+experiment on vLLM commit `1b2a666391f2a24228a1436b64d547c34cc6b6ce`.
+They are not added to automatic backend selection.
+
+```bash
+export ATOM_USE_FLYDSL_FP8_PREFILL_ATTN=1
+vllm serve "$MODEL" \
+    --attention-backend ROCM_AITER_FLYDSL_MLA \
+    --attention-config '{"mla_prefill_backend":"ROCM_AITER_FLYDSL_FP8"}'
+```
+
+Select both backends together. The native path does not require the external
+InferenceX plugin. The flag is read at backend construction; only the exact
+string `1` enables FP8. Unset or `0` keeps prefill attention in BF16 without
+importing the FlyDSL FP8 API.
+
+When enabled, cached chunks use FP8 only when maximum query length is at least
+512 and maximum KV length is at least 8192. Causal attention and smaller chunks
+use BF16. Supported FP8 shapes are checked through AITER's
+`flydsl_flash_attn_fp8_supported`; the measured target is MI355X, BF16 input,
+12 heads/rank, Q/K head size 192 and V head size 128.
+
+The native classes retain the experimental quantizer, per-forward Q reuse,
+native DCP reconstruction, and disabled main ASM prefill metadata. Expanded K/V
+remain BF16 before dynamic quantization. The flag does not configure weight
+quantization, and the measured recipe keeps `kv_b_proj` in BF16.
+
+This is a parity-validation draft. Native GPU output equivalence, a native
+serving smoke, and native performance have not been established. Results from
+the external plugin do not validate this native port.
